From fe4da3096ea25c4b4b5c40178528a22fa8982021 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:48:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Ookla speed test: ASUS's 102_40585 setup on the 3006.102.8
 line (102.8 line)

ASUS retired the Ookla embed key this line used on 2026-10-01. The 3006.102.10 line has had the
new setup since v3.6.0 (Asuswrt-Merlin 0c5d53820c7, "Merged with GPL 3006.102_40585", Eric
Sauvageau); this carries the same files to GT-BE98, GT-BE19000, BQ16 and BQ16 Pro:
shared/ookla_common.h + ookla_utils.c (the embed key by platform; an HND router outside the Wi-Fi 8
SDK gets the AXHND_A7 key), the quota (100 free tests, then 3 per 24 hours, once setup is complete;
rc applet ookla_quota_mon, nvram ookla_quota), the speed test page's quota notice, and the engine
build 40585 pairs with it (OOKLA-38000). web.c's Ookla block is the 3006.102.10 one, which keeps
Reaper's launch path (ookla_run, the kept stderr).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
